        "name": "USN-3993-2",
        "description": "USN-3993-1 fixed a vulnerability in curl. This update provides the corresponding update for Ubuntu 12.04 ESM and Ubuntu 14.04 ESM.  Original advisory details:   It was discovered that curl incorrectly handled memory when receiving data  from a TFTP server. A remote attacker could use this issue to cause curl to  crash, resulting in a denial of service, or possibly execute arbitrary  code. (CVE-2019-5436)",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2019-5436"
        ]
      },
